# Travelling in Russian: е́ду or е́зжу?
subtitle: "Say how you get around in Russian: е́ду for the trip you're on now, е́зжу for every day, на маши́не and на метро́, and е́здил for there and back."
tags: ["russian","verbs of motion","ездить","russian transport","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/verbs-of-motion","vocabulary/travel"]
thumb: "band \"Right now, or every day?\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Came and went in Russian: пришёл, ушёл","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/64-russian-motion-prefixes.cast"}

## Travelling in Russian: е́ду or е́зжу?
level: basic
heading: false

    icon masha size 140 set twemoji x 150 y 450 or ["girl"] icon_look picture of woman hidden true
